-------------------------------
Course Registration System
Z Notation Specification
-------------------------------

[STUDENT, COURSE]

--------------------------------
CourseRegistrationState
--------------------------------

students : ℙ STUDENT
courses : ℙ COURSE
enrollment : STUDENT ↔ COURSE
capacity : COURSE → ℕ

--------------------------------
State Invariants
--------------------------------

∀ s : STUDENT •
#({ c : COURSE | (s, c) ∈ enrollment }) ≤ 5

∀ c : COURSE •
#({ s : STUDENT | (s, c) ∈ enrollment }) ≤ capacity(c)

∀ s : STUDENT; c : COURSE •
(s, c) ∈ enrollment ⇒
s ∈ students ∧ c ∈ courses

--------------------------------
Explanation
--------------------------------

students → set of valid students
courses → set of valid courses
enrollment → relation between students and courses
capacity → maximum allowed students in each course

Invariant 1: A student can register in maximum 5 courses

Invariant 2: Registered students in a course cannot exceed capacity

Invariant 3: Every registration must involve valid student and course

--------------------------------------------------
Operation 1 : RegisterCourse
--------------------------------------------------

RegisterCourse
ΔCourseRegistrationState

s? : STUDENT
c? : COURSE

--------------------------------
Preconditions
--------------------------------

s? ∈ students

c? ∈ courses

(s?, c?) ∉ enrollment

#({ x : COURSE | (s?, x) ∈ enrollment }) < 5

#({ x : STUDENT | (x, c?) ∈ enrollment })
< capacity(c?)

--------------------------------
State Update
--------------------------------

enrollment' = enrollment ∪ { s? ↦ c? }

students' = students
courses' = courses
capacity' = capacity

--------------------------------------------------
Operation 2 : DropCourse
--------------------------------------------------

DropCourse
ΔCourseRegistrationState

s? : STUDENT
c? : COURSE

--------------------------------
Preconditions
--------------------------------

(s?, c?) ∈ enrollment

--------------------------------
State Update
--------------------------------

enrollment' = enrollment \ { s? ↦ c? }

students' = students
courses' = courses
capacity' = capacity

--------------------------------------------------
State Transition Modeling
--------------------------------------------------

Before RegisterCourse

students = { S1, S2 }

courses = { C1, C2 }

enrollment = { S1 ↦ C1 }

--------------------------------
Operation
--------------------------------

RegisterCourse(S2, C1)

--------------------------------
After RegisterCourse
--------------------------------

enrollment' = { S1 ↦ C1, S2 ↦ C1 }

--------------------------------------------------
Example of Invalid Transition
--------------------------------------------------

Invalid Operation:

RegisterCourse(S1, C1)

Explanation:
Reason: Student already registered in course
Result: Precondition fails
State does NOT change

--------------------------------------------------
Optional Error Operation
--------------------------------------------------

RegisterError
ΞCourseRegistrationState

s? : STUDENT
c? : COURSE

--------------------------------
Error Condition
--------------------------------

(s?, c?) ∈ enrollment

--------------------------------
Explanation
--------------------------------

Ξ means:
No state change occurs

Used to model invalid operations
and rejected registrations.